PRISM database migrations
==========================

PostgreSQL is migration-managed. From backend/, set DATABASE_URL and run:

    ./.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m alembic upgrade head

The API refuses to start on PostgreSQL when alembic_version is behind the
repository's single migration head. SQLite remains the zero-setup local demo:
application startup creates its tables and applies the narrow ensure_columns()
compatibility path documented in db/database.py.

Revision 65bc8695fadc is the autogenerated pre-governance baseline. Revision
2baf7d4bd8a2 adds the four governance tables. The follow-up safely adopts the
compatible table set created by the old PostgreSQL create_all() startup
behavior only after checking columns, types, nullability, primary keys,
indexes and foreign keys; it rejects partial or incompatible table sets.
Revision cf4271f204a3 adds the issuer-scoped identity_bindings table used by
the OIDC/RBAC principal resolver. It was autogenerated against a live
PostgreSQL database at revision 2baf7d4bd8a2 and is the current head.

The `-x baseline=true` filter in env.py exists only to reproduce the historical
baseline boundary. Do not use it for normal revisions or upgrades.
